\section{Vectors and Coordinate Systems}

\begin{frame}{What is a Vector?}

\textbf{Definition:}

A vector is a mathematical quantity that has both
\textbf{magnitude} and \textbf{direction}.

\vspace{0.3cm}

A vector can be represented using components.

For example,

\[
\mathbf{v}
=
\begin{bmatrix}
3\\
2
\end{bmatrix}
\]

means that the vector moves:

\begin{itemize}
    \item 3 units in the $x$ direction
    \item 2 units in the $y$ direction
\end{itemize}

\textbf{Example:}

If a person moves 3 m east and 2 m north, the displacement
can be represented by

\[
\mathbf{v}=(3,2)
\]

\end{frame}

