% =================================================
% COORDINATE SYSTEM
% =================================================

\begin{frame}{Coordinate System}

A coordinate system provides a reference for describing the
position of points and vectors.

\vspace{0.3cm}

In a two-dimensional coordinate system:

\[
P=(x,y)
\]

where:

\begin{itemize}
    \item $x$ represents the horizontal coordinate.
    \item $y$ represents the vertical coordinate.
\end{itemize}

\textbf{Example:}

For

\[
P=(3,2)
\]

we move 3 units along the $x$-axis and 2 units along the
$y$-axis.

\end{frame}

