\section{Applications}

\begin{frame}{Applications of Linear Algebra}

Linear algebra is widely used in computing and data science.

\begin{itemize}

\item \textbf{Machine Learning}

Vectors represent data and matrices represent transformations.

\item \textbf{Computer Graphics}

Matrices are used for rotation, scaling, translation and projection.

\item \textbf{Computer Vision}

Images can be represented using matrices.

\item \textbf{Data Science}

Datasets can be represented as matrices.

\item \textbf{Deep Learning}

Neural network operations involve matrix multiplication.

\end{itemize}

\end{frame}

