% SUMMARY
% =================================================

\begin{frame}{Summary}

\begin{itemize}

\item Vectors represent magnitude and direction.

\item Coordinate systems provide a way to represent vectors
and points.

\item Vector operations include addition and scalar multiplication.

\item Linear combinations generate new vectors.

\item Span describes the set of vectors that can be generated.

\item A basis provides an independent coordinate system.

\item Matrices represent linear transformations.

\item Determinants describe area and volume scaling.

\item Inverse matrices reverse transformations.

\item Column space and null space describe important properties
of matrices.

\item Dot products measure projection and orthogonality.

\item Cross products produce perpendicular vectors in $\mathbb R^3$.

\item Eigenvectors preserve their direction under a transformation.

\item Vector spaces provide the mathematical framework for all
these concepts.

\end{itemize}

\end{frame}

